  ],
  "slug": "adna-alignment-sensitivity-dbd7",
  "summary": "New aligners, an assembler, a k-mer counter, a placement tool, and accelerators each report large speed or memory gains over established baselines.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reducing the cost of core sequence-processing kernels through algorithmic redesign or algorithm–hardware co-design. For alignment, minibwa combines BWA-MEM seeding with minimap2 chaining and is reported ~4x faster than BWA-MEM at comparable accuracy. lWFA and bidirectional lBiWFA extend wavefront alignment to exact local alignment in O(sN) time with reduced memory. VEGA (a RISC-V vector-extension co-design, up to 15.1x over Ara2-RVV) and Motivo (a motif-indexed ASIC for sequence-to-graph mapping) move DP and graph alignment into hardware. Gallifrey uses locally consistent de Bruijn graphs for HiFi draft assembly, reported >6x faster than rust-mdbg with 2x less memory. Tuna revisits sort versus hash k-mer counting with a cost model and minimizer partitioning, outperforming KMC3. New in this set, gPlace extends the theme to phylogenetic placement, matching pplacer output exactly with >3-fold lower memory and >30-fold faster runtime.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
